 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Status Panel -- Overtyping Fields        !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                  }
}
}  Two fields of a job can be changed by typing over them and pressing
}  Enter. SDSF gives JES2 the command that changes the job.
}
{  PRTY  }The priority: a number. JES2 checks the range ($T with P=).
{  DEST  }The destination of the job's output: LOCAL, or Rn for remote n
}         ($R ALL with D=).
}
}  You can overtype fields on several lines at once. SDSF checks all of
}  them first: if one is not good, none is changed, the values you typed
}  stay, the cursor goes to the field in error and the panel says why:
}
{    FIELD NOT NUMERIC          }PRTY is not a number
{    INVALID DESTINATION NAME   }DEST is neither LOCAL nor Rn
}
}  Changing a job needs update access to it; your own jobs you may always
}  change.
}
}
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: Status panel help   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHSTM
  &ZUP = ISFHST
)END
